[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/441943134","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/4359#issuecomment-441943134","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/4359","id":441943134,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ0MTk0MzEzNA==","user":{"login":"sqlalchemy-bot","id":36047385,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MDQ3Mzg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36047385?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2018-11-06T15:35:31Z","updated_at":"2018-11-27T06:25:35Z","body":"**Michael Bayer ([@zzzeek](https://github.com/zzzeek)) wrote:**\n\nOK here's a much more succinct case\n\n\n```\nfrom sqlalchemy import *\nfrom sqlalchemy.orm import *\nfrom sqlalchemy.ext.declarative import declarative_base\n\nBase = declarative_base()\n\n\nclass A(Base):\n    __tablename__ = 'a'\n\n    id = Column(Integer, primary_key=True)\n    bs = relationship(\"B\", backref=\"a\")\n\n\nclass B(Base):\n    __tablename__ = 'b'\n    id = Column(Integer, primary_key=True)\n    a_id = Column(ForeignKey(\"a.id\"))\n\ne = create_engine(\"sqlite://\", echo=True)\nBase.metadata.create_all(e)\n\ns = Session(e)\n\ns.add(A(bs=[B()]))\ns.commit()\n\n\ndef foo(s):\n    a = s.query(A).first()\n    return B.a == a\n\nb1 = s.query(B).first()\nb1.a\ncrit = foo(s)\n\ns.expire(b1.a)\ns.expire(b1)\n\nprint(crit.left.callable())\n\n\n```\n\nI think the deferred nature of the comparison needs to be liberalized such that it memoizes the immediate comparison state and uses that if the object is expired.\n","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/441943134/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"sqlalchemy-bot","id":36047385,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MDQ3Mzg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36047385?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/441943136","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/4359#issuecomment-441943136","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/4359","id":441943136,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ0MTk0MzEzNg==","user":{"login":"sqlalchemy-bot","id":36047385,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MDQ3Mzg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36047385?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2018-11-06T15:56:32Z","updated_at":"2018-11-27T06:25:35Z","body":"**Michael Bayer ([@zzzeek](https://github.com/zzzeek)) wrote:**\n\nthis is going to be great.  the whole tradition of these loader callables being deferred is almost never needed and the purpose of it is to suit using unflushed objects.   so we will just get the value immediately, as is almost always what people want, and only if that is None do we try again.  it's a big change but will make things work a lot more simply.\n\n\n```\ndiff --git a/lib/sqlalchemy/orm/relationships.py b/lib/sqlalchemy/orm/relationships.py\nindex 818f1c0ae2..8ab64cd66e 100644\n--- a/lib/sqlalchemy/orm/relationships.py\n+++ b/lib/sqlalchemy/orm/relationships.py\n@@ -1425,7 +1425,16 @@ class RelationshipProperty(StrategizedProperty):\n         return criterion\n \n     def _get_attr_w_warn_on_none(self, column, fn, *arg, **kw):\n+        # in the vast majority of cases, this is the value\n+        # we want to use.   The edge case served by having a deferred\n+        # callable is that the object has been added to a session but\n+        # is not flushed yet, in which case we re-evaluate the callable\n+        # a second time.\n+        pre_exec_value = fn(*arg, **kw)\n+\n         def _go():\n+            if pre_exec_value is not None:\n+                return pre_exec_value\n             value = fn(*arg, **kw)\n             if value is None:\n                 util.warn(\ndiff --git a/test/orm/test_dynamic.py b/test/orm/test_dynamic.py\nindex 5c514ff1a5..3cbf651716 100644\n--- a/test/orm/test_dynamic.py\n+++ b/test/orm/test_dynamic.py\n@@ -504,13 +504,12 @@ class UOWTest(\n \n         u1.addresses.append(Address(email_address='a2'))\n \n+        # this was not true before the change\n+        assert 'id' in u1.__dict__\n+\n         self.assert_sql_execution(\n             testing.db,\n             sess.flush,\n-            CompiledSQL(\n-                \"SELECT users.id AS users_id, users.name AS users_name \"\n-                \"FROM users WHERE users.id = :param_1\",\n-                lambda ctx: [{\"param_1\": u1_id}]),\n             CompiledSQL(\n                 \"INSERT INTO addresses (user_id, email_address) \"\n                 \"VALUES (:user_id, :email_address)\",\n@@ -536,6 +535,9 @@ class UOWTest(\n \n         u1.addresses.remove(a2)\n \n+        # this was not true before the change\n+        assert 'id' in u1.__dict__\n+\n         self.assert_sql_execution(\n             testing.db,\n             sess.flush,\n@@ -549,11 +551,7 @@ class UOWTest(\n                 \"UPDATE addresses SET user_id=:user_id WHERE addresses.id = \"\n                 \":addresses_id\",\n                 lambda ctx: [{'addresses_id': a2_id, 'user_id': None}]\n-            ),\n-            CompiledSQL(\n-                \"SELECT users.id AS users_id, users.name AS users_name \"\n-                \"FROM users WHERE users.id = :param_1\",\n-                lambda ctx: [{\"param_1\": u1_id}]),\n+            )\n         )\n \n     def test_rollback(self):\n\n```\n","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/441943136/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"sqlalchemy-bot","id":36047385,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MDQ3Mzg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36047385?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/441943144","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/4359#issuecomment-441943144","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/4359","id":441943144,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ0MTk0MzE0NA==","user":{"login":"sqlalchemy-bot","id":36047385,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MDQ3Mzg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36047385?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy-bot","follo